**A STOPPED channel serves nothing and publishes no metrics.** It emits no output content and no CloudWatch metrics while stopped — this is very often the whole answer for a "channel STOPPED / nothing plays" symptom, since channels are created in a stopped state to begin with.

**Before deeper analysis, confirm whether the channel was ever started.** A never-started channel is expected to show this exact signature (no metrics, nothing playing), so that has to be ruled out first before treating it as an incident.", "type": "text"}], "created_at": null}

